# BBS Photon Addon — agent map

You are an expert developer for **BBS Photon Addon**, a NeoForge addon that exposes [Photon Editor / Photon2](https://github.com/LowDragMC/Photon) particle FX as a BBS form for [BBS CML Edition](https://github.com/ElGatoPro300/BBS-CML-EDITION). This open-source repo is also a **reference implementation** for authors writing BBS addons.

## How to use this document

This file is a **short always-on map**, not a full manual.

1. Use the paragraphs below to recognize which subsystem a request touches.
2. **Before changing that area**, open the linked deep-dive under `docs/architecture/`.
3. For BBS host contracts (forms, Values, events), prefer the public addon guide: [BBS CML `docs/ADDONS.md`](https://github.com/ElGatoPro300/BBS-CML-EDITION/blob/master/docs/ADDONS.md) — functional spec, not code to paste.
4. Obey FEATURE-RULES Part 1 + Part 2 (`.cursor/rules/` or `.agents/rules/`).

Operational checklists and pitfalls live in the deep-dives — keep them out of this file.

## Porting / dependency bumps

- Do **not** bump Photon, BBS, NeoForge, or invent a Fabric-only target unless the developer **explicitly** asks.
- When a Photon `2.2.x` bump is requested (target pin: `mc1.21.1-2.2.7-neoforge`), adapt adapter/bridge code and update `docs/architecture/photon2-compat-plan.md`. Domain `PhotonForm` Values should stay stable.

## Hard rules (always)

- UI strings use BBS `L10n` / `IKey`; never hardcode user-facing text.
- Persistent form fields use the BBS `Value` system; do not rename `photon_fx` / `paused` without a migration plan.
- Domain (`forms/`) stays free of Minecraft and Photon imports; Photon FX calls live in adapter/bridges.
- Respect Iris/shadow constraints when drawing FX in the world or film viewport.
- Bugfixes stay surgical; do not further inflate `PhotonFormRenderer` — extract instead.
- This addon targets **NeoForge 1.21.1** (+ Connector) only unless explicitly told otherwise.

